								<r3d:remarks>Pulsed SILAC (pSILAC) is a variation of the SILAC method where the labelled amino acids are added to the growth medium for only a short period of time. This allows monitoring differences in de novo protein production rather than raw concentration. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stable_isotope_labeling_by_amino_acids_in_cell_culture
1 Sep 2014: the group of Miguel Andrade is moving to the Institute of Molecular Biology in Mainz from the Max Delbrück Center for Molecular Medicine in Berlin</r3d:remarks>
